WWP IT RUNBOOK RB-03 - LINUX SERVER PATCHING
Owner: Kevin Tran (Systems Administrator)          Rev. 2026-02-10
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Scope: Corporate and DMZ Linux servers (ww-web01, ww-fs01, ww-it01).
OT DMZ / SCADA servers (ww-hist01, ww-jump01, ww-hmi01, ww-eng01) are
patched ONLY by Engineering/Hydra Controls during scheduled vendor visits.
Do not touch them from IT.

Window: 2nd Tuesday + 1 week, 18:00-21:00. Post in #it-changes first.

Steps
 1. Confirm the nightly config backup on ww-it01 ran
      ls -l /var/backups/it/
 2. Snapshot the VM in the hypervisor console (name: pre-patch-YYYYMMDD).
 3. On the server:
      sudo apt update && apt list --upgradable
      sudo apt -y upgrade
      sudo needrestart -r l
 4. Reboot if a new kernel or libc was installed.
 5. Verify services:
      ww-fs01   systemctl status smbd; smbclient -L //localhost -U <you>
      ww-web01  curl -I http://localhost/ ; check /reports page loads
      ww-it01   systemctl status cron ssh
 6. Delete the snapshot after 7 days if no issues.

Known issues
 - ww-web01: the CIFS mount of \\ww-fs01\Public for the CCR page sometimes
   comes up before networking; `mount -a` fixes it.
 - ww-fs01: after samba upgrades re-run `testparm -s` and make sure the
   IT$ share is still hidden (browseable = no).
